2:06:09.764829+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-m0.1","local_name":"bob-cli-m0.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-m0","agent_clan_generation":"20261115200254","bead_id":"bob-cli-m0.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-m0[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Ctrl+W window prefix for Obsidian vertical splits[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]In Bob's Obsidian, Ctrl+W followed by a key focuses, moves, and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]creates main-area splits from the keyboard. h/l focus the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]neighbouring split, H/L move the current tab into, out of, or [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]across splits (creating and collapsing splits as needed) without [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]losing its editor state, and a calm, theme-native hint shows [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]exactly what each key will do.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]obsidian_ctrl_w_window_prefix.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/obsidian_ctrl_w_window_prefix.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-m0[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-m0/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Real-Obsidian layout and keyboard spike[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]spike[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]spike: build the window-prefix CDP e2e harness and prove lossless [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cross-group tab moves, split create/collapse, and keyboard precedence in[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]real Obsidian.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Pure layout model, planners, key table, and view model[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]model[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]model: add Obsidian-free fragments that turn a layout snapshot into [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]focus/move/split plans, key normalization, arming verdicts, and the hint[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]view model.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Live layout adapter and lossless executor[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]actions[dim] · [dim][/dim]after spike, model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]actions: build the live snapshot adapter and executor that focuses, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]joins, creates, collapses, and duplicates splits with invariants, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rollback, and an API canary.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Ring, card, minimap, and motion painter[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]hint[dim] · [dim][/dim]after model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]hint: paint the armed ring, key-cap badge, hint card with minimap, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]nudges, pulses, and receipts from the view model, with a light/dark [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]preview harness.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Ctrl+W prefix state machine[/bold #D7AFFF]                                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]prefix[dim] · [dim][/dim]after actions, hint[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prefix: wire the capture listener, armed keymap scope, arming gate, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dispatch, cancel paths, and two-tier hint timing into a reliable Ctrl+W [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF